title The prices differ because the promises do
prompt kg -- fetch sbase and ubase next
obs Licenses read from their own files rather than repeated: sbase is plain MIT, ubase is MIT/X Consortium. The June inventory said MIT/ISC for both, which is close and not exact, and the correction is recorded rather than quietly applied.
obs The elder claim was short enough to hold in the eye. Now it is a number: 98 commands, 18,869 lines of C, median command 91 lines. A claim that survives measurement is worth more after the measurement than before it.
think The finding is not sbase alone, it is sbase read against the two fetched earlier today. cat is 52 lines with one flag here, 68 with four in toybox, and 796 with eleven plus a platform directory carrying a Windows port in uutils. That is a 15x span on the simplest command in the family.
obs And none of it is waste, which is the part worth writing down. Each project pays for a different promise: sbase for portability by declining to do what is not portable, toybox for a whole userland in one binary, uutils for exact GNU compatibility across five operating systems. The prices differ because the promises do -- and only three side by side make each price legible. One study could not have shown this; three could.
obs sbase has no awk, and after dawk and toybox that reads as agreement rather than absence. sed at 1,738 lines is the largest thing sbase attempts, so even the project built on subtraction finds the text-processing tools are the hard half. Three independent projects, one conclusion.
obs Why this is the model for a Rye base suite, stated as fit rather than preference: TAME asks for bounded everything, asserted invariants, short functions named with a verb. A 91-line median command written portable-by-subtraction has few places left to hide an unnamed bound, which is a structural argument rather than a taste one.
obs The gratitude page read B/83 on its first pass with 29 percent negative sentences -- the framing habit that caught uutils and toybox did not recur. Leading with what a thing IS appears to be learnable within a day.
obs The card closed at five bytes of headroom. That is the one-byte signal from this morning arriving again, and the raise to 32,768 has been spent in a single day by five fetch studies and a naming study. Named for Keaton rather than fixed: the live front now wants a shelf the way REDS has one, since condensing served blocks is reaching the point where it removes meaning rather than words.
loom sbase license=MIT ubase_license=MIT/X commands=98 lines=18869 median=91
loom cat_comparison sbase=52/1flag toybox=68/4 uutils=796/11+windows
file gratitude/sbase the submodule, whole and unmodified
file gratitude/ubase the Linux-facing complement, whole and unmodified
file gratitude/suckless-sbase-ubase.md the thanks, and the three-way comparison that makes each price legible
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- ripgrep is last in the fetch order; and the card wants a live-front shelf, since five bytes of headroom means the next lap deletes meaning rather than words
